WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:03.316
(energetic piano music)

00:00:04.913 --> 00:00:06.395
- We're gonna try all
these different flavors,

00:00:06.395 --> 00:00:08.095
we're gonna guess what they are.

00:00:08.095 --> 00:00:09.202
(ringing bell)

00:00:10.158 --> 00:00:12.756
(chips rustle)

00:00:13.025 --> 00:00:14.210
- Smells like a spice rack.

00:00:14.505 --> 00:00:16.136
- Whoa.
- It smells like a deli.

00:00:16.371 --> 00:00:17.831
- I don't know how I feel about this.

00:00:17.874 --> 00:00:19.200
- It, like, changes flavors.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:19.842
- Mm-hmm.

00:00:19.842 --> 00:00:20.862
- Kind of, right?

00:00:20.862 --> 00:00:22.933
- They really nailed the
rye and sauerkraut flavor.

00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:23.656
- Yeah.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.281
- Tastes like cheese, there's
like this big cheese--

00:00:25.281 --> 00:00:26.338
- Sour cheese.

00:00:26.338 --> 00:00:28.137
- It does taste like a Reuben.

00:00:28.137 --> 00:00:30.477
(chips rustle)

00:00:30.477 --> 00:00:33.004
- These chips are big
first of all, that's great.

00:00:33.004 --> 00:00:35.103
- Oh, man. That smells like...

00:00:35.103 --> 00:00:35.951
- Fish.

00:00:35.951 --> 00:00:37.057
- That doesn't taste like anything.

00:00:37.057 --> 00:00:38.548
- Reminds me of an Italian restaurant.

00:00:38.548 --> 00:00:40.465
- Yeah it tastes like
an Italian restaurant.

00:00:40.465 --> 00:00:41.281
Tastes like pasta chips.

00:00:41.281 --> 00:00:43.213
- Do we have to, can we
just stop right here?

00:00:43.213 --> 00:00:44.300
I'm done. This is it.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:44.890
(laughs)

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.569
- We're gonna finish out the
bowl and we'll be right back.

00:00:46.569 --> 00:00:49.852
(chips rustle)

00:00:49.852 --> 00:00:50.701
- Wow these are brown.

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:52.669
- These look like it's gonna
be a really strong flavor.

00:00:52.669 --> 00:00:53.308
- Yeah.

00:00:53.308 --> 00:00:54.018
- Oh!

00:00:54.018 --> 00:00:55.419
- Is this chip like thicker to you?

00:00:55.419 --> 00:00:56.216
And like harder?

00:00:56.216 --> 00:00:56.626
- Mm-hm.

00:00:56.626 --> 00:00:58.386
- It tastes kinda like a salad to me.

00:00:58.386 --> 00:01:00.016
- There's like, olive.

00:01:00.016 --> 00:01:01.286
- There's like a pickle element of it.

00:01:01.286 --> 00:01:02.567
- That's so good, though.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:04.317
- Almost too much for a chip.

00:01:04.317 --> 00:01:07.345
(chips rustle)

00:01:07.345 --> 00:01:09.813
- They all smell the same, what the,

00:01:09.813 --> 00:01:11.257
I'm like mad now.

00:01:11.257 --> 00:01:12.421
- Ranch
- Meat

00:01:12.421 --> 00:01:12.903
- Ranch?

00:01:12.903 --> 00:01:14.389
(laughs)

00:01:14.389 --> 00:01:15.372
- I went with meat.

00:01:15.372 --> 00:01:17.713
- They taste like upper-class
sour cream and onion.

00:01:17.713 --> 00:01:18.237
- Yeah.

00:01:18.237 --> 00:01:18.907
- Chips.

00:01:18.907 --> 00:01:20.073
- It tastes like grabbing
a handful of meat

00:01:20.073 --> 00:01:21.081
and putting it in your mouth.

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.001
- Definitely a hint of gravy.

00:01:23.001 --> 00:01:24.026
- Is that pepper?

00:01:24.026 --> 00:01:25.261
- Yeah, there's definitely pepper on it.

00:01:25.261 --> 00:01:26.667
- There's something comforting about them.

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:27.106
- Yeah.

00:01:27.106 --> 00:01:27.926
- A little homey.

00:01:27.926 --> 00:01:29.270
- I think we both agree that
these are truffle, right?

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:30.084
- Oh yeah.

00:01:30.084 --> 00:01:31.347
- I thought this would be easy

00:01:31.347 --> 00:01:32.356
and it's actually really difficult.

00:01:32.356 --> 00:01:33.924
- Definitely the biscuits and gravy here.

00:01:33.924 --> 00:01:34.664
- We're right!
(bell rings)

00:01:34.664 --> 00:01:36.017
- Woot woot.

00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:36.355
- This is our guess.

00:01:36.355 --> 00:01:37.632
(bell rings)

00:01:37.632 --> 00:01:38.268
(bell rings)

00:01:38.268 --> 00:01:39.638
- Nice.

00:01:39.638 --> 00:01:40.746
(buzzer sounds)

00:01:40.746 --> 00:01:42.027
- Are you kidding me?

00:01:42.027 --> 00:01:42.713
- No!
- What?!

00:01:42.713 --> 00:01:43.980
- - Not a chance in hell!

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:44.902
(bell rings)

00:01:44.902 --> 00:01:45.692
- Yeah!

00:01:45.692 --> 00:01:49.316
- You're telling me that
this is how it should go.

00:01:51.096 --> 00:01:52.862
- I'm gonna stare at this one and eat.

00:01:52.862 --> 00:01:54.201
- God damn it, you're right.

00:01:54.201 --> 00:01:56.842
- I think this might be my
favorite, the biscuits and gravy.

00:01:56.842 --> 00:01:58.507
- Nah, man.
- Baby, no, wrong.

00:01:58.507 --> 00:01:59.724
- It's all about that Reuben.

00:01:59.724 --> 00:02:00.464
- Your choice is wrong.

00:02:00.464 --> 00:02:02.515
- I think it's pretty apparent
which one's a favorite.

00:02:02.585 --> 00:02:04.227
- I feel like we live in the future,

00:02:04.237 --> 00:02:06.390
and that you can eat a
sandwich in chip form.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:09.379
- Oh! I wish Lays would
just make bags of meat.

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:10.360
(laughs)

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.576
That tasted like other things.

00:02:12.576 --> 00:02:15.082
Like instead of, leave
the potato behind, Lays!

00:02:15.082 --> 00:02:17.724
Just give us roast beef
that tastes like chicken.

00:02:17.724 --> 00:02:18.762
How fun!

